      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Order as written:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. The usual single-dose maximum is 800 mg. The over-the-counter limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is double the maximum daily dose. It carries a high risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n1. **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n2. **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, for typical analgesia.\n3. **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily.\n4. **Another regimen.** If so, please give the dose and frequency, and I can add an order note with the indication.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
